From 291d94a536b64097dc206862e38ea59397ac7923 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 15:02:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Close the connection leak, and bridge a supplier advisory to
 a CRA Article 14 intake
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

WHY
  Two defects and one integration.

  The leak: sqlite3's context manager commits, it does not close. Every
  EvidenceLedger and AccountStore construction leaked a file handle — 210
  ResourceWarnings a test run, and an exhausted file table under load in a
  served deployment.

  The test: a plain file copy of a WAL-mode database leaves the write-ahead
  log behind, so the copy arrived without its records and, on a freshly
  written ledger, without the schema.

  The integration: Article 14(2)(a) gives a manufacturer 24 hours to file an
  early warning naming the Member States the product was made available in.
  Everything else on that form can be written under pressure. That list
  cannot — it is an inventory question whose answer lives in four
  spreadsheets. The fleet already knows it.

WHAT
  src/assurance/evidence/ledger.py    close explicitly; snapshot_to() does a
                                       WAL-safe backup so a copied ledger is a
                                       whole ledger
  src/assurance/billing/accounts.py   same close
  src/assurance/machinery/manifest.py MachineIdentity.country, ISO 3166-1
                                       alpha-2, refused if malformed
  src/assurance/collect/*             --country carried through collection
  src/assurance/bridge/art14.py       advisory + fleet -> Article 14 intake
  src/assurance/bridge/cli.py         assurance bridge art14 ... --open
  deploy/assurance/BRIDGE.md          the 24-hour field, and what is refused

CUSTOMER VALUE
  "2 affected machines in 2 Member States: DE, IT" — assembled in a second,
  with the serial numbers it was built from as its evidence, at the moment a
  manufacturer has 24 hours and no list. Nobody else can do it because nobody
  else has both the fleet and the register.

RISK
  This is the surface where over-reach becomes a false regulatory statement,
  so the bridge does the inventory and refuses the judgement. No track is set:
  an advisory naming a defect is not by itself an actively exploited
  vulnerability. No awareness timestamp is set: awareness is a determination
  after an assessment, not the arrival of an email. Only machines matched by
  artefact hash count toward field 5; a label-only or contradictory match
  contributes no territory and is listed as needing a person. A machine with
  no country recorded blocks the field and the command exits non-zero, because
  a filing with a wrong field 5 is worse than a late one. And the Article 14
  register still refuses a filing until a person records both decisions —
  asserted in the tests.

  MachineIdentity.country changes the manifest content hash. Done now, while
  there is no installed base.

ROLLBACK
  git revert this commit. The country field and the two close() fixes are the
  only changes outside assurance/bridge.

TESTS
  560 passed (30 new), ruff clean, and 1 warning where there were 211.

SUCCESS CONDITION
  One manufacturer answers field 5 from a command instead of a phone call, on
  a day when the clock is running.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
